## MCP stdio server VM args
##
## -noshell: no Erlang shell — essential for stdio MCP servers:
##   - prevents the shell from competing for stdin
##   - prevents shell/REPL output from polluting stdout
##   - the `user` I/O server is still bound to fd 0/1
##
## Do NOT use -noinput: the transport must read stdin.
##
## The `user` registered process is the I/O server bound to fd 0/1
## under -noshell. The transport reads via io:get_line(user, "") and
## writes via io:put_chars(user, Data).

-sname simple
-noshell
